---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="About" currentPath="/about">
	<section class="about narrow container">
		<p class="breadcrumb">// about</p>
		<h1>About the lab</h1>

		<p>
			LLM Tune Lab is a technical notebook for people who work with open-weight language models — the ones doing the fine-tuning, the quantizing, the eval-running, and the debugging at 2 AM when the inference server silently OOMs.
		</p>

		<h2>What we cover</h2>

		<ul>
			<li><strong>Local inference</strong> — running large models on consumer hardware, quantization recipes, serving setups</li>
			<li><strong>Models</strong> — architecture deep-dives, training tricks, speculative decoding, context length engineering</li>
			<li><strong>Tooling</strong> — eval harnesses, training pipelines, debug workflows, the infrastructure that makes everything else possible</li>
		</ul>

		<h2>Why this exists</h2>

		<p>
			Most LLM content is either high-level product announcements or low-level research papers. The middle ground — the practical, tested, "here's what actually worked on my hardware" territory — is underserved. This lab fills that gap.
		</p>

		<p>
			Every post is based on direct experience. No sponsored content, no affiliate links, no "top 10 AI tools" listicles.
		</p>

		<h2>Get in touch</h2>

		<p>
			Find us on <a href="https://github.com/llmtunelab">GitHub</a> or subscribe to the <a href="/rss.xml">RSS feed</a> to stay updated.
		</p>
	</section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
	.about {
		padding-top: 3rem;
		padding-bottom: 3rem;
	}

	.breadcrumb {
		font-size: 0.85rem;
		color: var(--text-muted);
		margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
	}

	.about h1 {
		font-size: 2.25rem;
		margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
	}

	.about h2 {
		font-size: 1.35rem;
		margin-top: 2.5rem;
		margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
	}

	.about p {
		margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
		line-height: 1.7;
		color: var(--text-secondary);
	}

	.about ul {
		padding-left: 1.25rem;
		margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
	}

	.about li {
		margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
		line-height: 1.6;
		color: var(--text-secondary);
	}

	.about strong {
		color: var(--text-primary);
	}

	.about a {
		color: var(--accent);
		text-decoration: underline;
		text-underline-offset: 2px;
	}

	.about a:hover {
		color: var(--text-primary);
	}
</style>
